(pass) scrypt matches RFC 7914 12 [175.45ms]
(pass) base64url round-trips every length and refuses anything not strict [8.26ms]
(pass) seal/open round-trips text and 4 KB of bytes, and each seal is different [26.45ms]
(pass) a sealed message that was altered, cut, or sealed to another key is refused, never garbage [18.15ms]
(pass) bundle round-trips at the default cost, and unlock finishes in under 6 s [9633.09ms]
(pass) the header carries m, t, p and a fresh salt, readable without the passphrase [1522.29ms]
(pass) a wrong passphrase fails cleanly [164.06ms]
(pass) a tampered bundle is refused: damaged in copying, altered on purpose, or asking for too much work [207.91ms]
(pass) a bundle of an unknown version, or not a bundle at all, says so [31.97ms]
(pass) a bundle pasted with line breaks and spaces unlocks, and the passphrase is Unicode-normalised [64.57ms]
(pass) the async pair round-trips, and gives byte-identical bundles to the sync pair for the same salt [3019.69ms]
(pass) without setTimeout the async pair falls back to the sync path, with the same output [104.24ms]
(pass) the async pair fails with the same faults as the sync pair [222.86ms]
(pass) passphrase strength scores and explains, and only warns [3.71ms]

